Description: VeltOS Update: new VeltOS releases on an installed PC
 Every VeltOS release on GitHub carries the ISO for new installations and
 all of VeltOS' packages with a package index signed by VeltOS' archive
 key. This package makes that index a package source of the PC
 (/etc/apt/sources.list.d/veltos.sources with the archive key, written
 by a system timer while the newest release carries the signed index), so
 a new release reaches installed PCs as package updates: changed and new
 VeltOS apps, the system's own parts, with the user's files, settings and
 programs left as they are.
 .
 A user timer looks for a new release and other updates once a day and
 shows a notification; VeltOS Settings > VeltOS Update shows what is new
 (the release's notes, in English or Turkish) and installs it.
